Subject: [PATCH] VIX from Cboe's official daily close (FRED as fallback); FRED
 fetches try Python's default agent first

Owner 2026-11-06 17:27 approved. The relay's 11/06 14:59 run lost VIXCLS to a
FRED timeout, and FRED republishes the Cboe close about a day late, so the
site still showed 11/04 (16.61) after the 11/05 spike. The relay now reads
Cboe's VIX_History.csv first (11/06 17:28 Taipei it already had the 11/05
close 28.18; past closes equal FRED's) and falls back to FRED VIXCLS with a
note. FRED requests in the keyless and cross-market relays try Python's
default User-Agent first, then the named one; broken downloads are retried
up to four times with 5/10/20 s waits. The site reads the row unchanged.

